{%- comment -%}
  Prints "yes" when every {token} in a text has something to show, and "no" when one of them would come out empty.
  A text with {date} needs the Christmas dates to be switched on and not past; {returns}, {free_shipping} and {shipping_fee}
  need a value in Theme settings > Christmas and delivery. Use it to hide a badge or a trust point instead of showing half a sentence.

  Accepts:
  - text: {String} the text that may contain tokens
  - season: {String} what the christmas-state snippet printed: 'open', 'closed' or 'off'

  Usage (a snippet cannot return a value, so capture what it prints):
  {% capture ready %}{% render 'tokens-ready', text: block.settings.text, season: season %}{% endcapture %}
  {% if ready == 'yes' %} ... {% endif %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign ready = 'yes'
  if text contains '{date}' or text contains '{short_date}'
    unless season == 'open'
      assign ready = 'no'
    endunless
  endif
  if text contains '{returns}' and settings.returns_days == blank
    assign ready = 'no'
  endif
  if text contains '{free_shipping}'
    unless settings.free_shipping_threshold > 0
      assign ready = 'no'
    endunless
  endif
  if text contains '{shipping_fee}'
    unless settings.shipping_fee > 0
      assign ready = 'no'
    endunless
  endif
  echo ready
-%}
